      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I’ve figured out a workaround for now—so long as there is no intersection “by default”/when the avatar loads in, the bug won’t happen. So now I just have my affected Sender/Receiver pairs offset from each other in Unity, then I use an animation in my FX layer to scoot them back into the correct position and hold them there.\n\n e.g. I shift all my Senders by ten meters along their local Y axes in Unity, then I record an animation of shifting them back the ten meters. They load in with the Contacts held apart, then immediately move them together; this way nothing gets bugged, and fixed avatars no longer need to be reset after world switching.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
